  "notes": "USAGE: {何|なに}か is used to refer to an unspecified thing. It can mean \"something\" in statements or \"anything\" in questions and conditionals.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{何|なに}か{食|た}べる (to eat something)\n・{何|なに}か{飲|の}む (to drink something)\n・{何|なに}かあったら (if anything happens)\n・{何|なに}か{用|よう}ですか (Can I help you?/Do you need something?)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n・{何|なに}も (nothing - with negative)\n・{誰|だれ}か (someone)\n・どこか (somewhere)\n・いつか (sometime)",
